 performing oversampling of the minority class using SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique), which resulted in the equal distribution of both the classes (0 and 1). Used the following modules in Python-Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, matplotlib, Imbalanced-learn Logistic Regression gave AUC=0.95, but the precision was very low (0.08). So, I tried Random Forests and it gave AUC=0.94 and precision=0.85 (with 'gini' criterion) and AUC=0.92 & precision=0.83 (with 'entropy' criterion). Measured performance metrics-accuracy, precision, recall, AUC and plotted ROC curve Used the following modules in Python-Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, matplotlib, Imbalanced-learn","topics":[],"score":234457,"global_rank":94621},{"name":"GordonsBeard/cafe-flask","owner":"GordonsBeard","html_url":"https://github.com/GordonsBeard/cafe-flask","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":1,"language":"Python","description":"Cafe of Broken Dreams website on flask","topics":[],"score":234454,"global_rank":94625},{"name":"jiayuasu/Synthetic-data-generator","owner":"jiayuasu","html_url":"https://github.com/jiayuasu/Synthetic-data-generator","stars":2,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Synthetic data generator for generating uniform/normal/exponential distribution data","topics":[],"score":234447,"global_rank":94638},{"name":"bxtbold/trajectory-executor","owner":"bxtbold","html_url":"https://github.com/bxtbold/trajectory-executor","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":3,"language":"Python","description":"A lightweight executor for offline, time-based joint trajectories in robotic applications.","topics":[],"score":234446,"global_rank":94640},{"name":"kkrausse/boookkeeping-demo","owner":"kkrausse","html_url":"https://github.com/kkrausse/boookkeeping-demo","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"sample bookkeeping app","topics":[],"score":234446,"global_rank":94645},{"name":"mdot2x3/wgups-routing-program-implementation",